%% D1 M1.4 — What happens when you run kubectl apply
%% Use: live-demo slide. Animate one step at a time.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as kubectl
    participant A as kube-apiserver
    participant E as etcd
    participant C as controller-manager
    participant S as kube-scheduler
    participant K as kubelet (m02)
    participant R as containerd

    U->>A: POST /apis/apps/v1/.../deployments
    A->>A: authenticate → authorise → admission
    A->>E: persist Deployment
    E-->>A: committed
    A-->>U: 201 Created
    Note over U,A: kubectl is DONE. Nothing is running yet.

    C->>A: watch: new Deployment
    C->>A: create ReplicaSet
    C->>A: watch: new ReplicaSet
    C->>A: create 3 Pods (nodeName empty)

    S->>A: watch: unscheduled Pods
    S->>S: filter nodes → score → pick
    S->>A: bind Pod → node m02

    K->>A: watch: Pods where nodeName = m02
    K->>R: create container (CRI)
    R-->>K: running
    K->>A: update Pod status → Running
